      "evidence": "Successful parse definitions take io and aux addrspace(1) pointers plus scalar offsets, rather than FullMemory*. Both successful a.g.lto.ll and a.o.3.ll contain zero i8** text occurrences. Attention v2 stops in the reflow command reading a.g.ld.5.gdce.bc and intending to write a.g.lto.bc. Neither that output nor a.g.2.prechk.bc/a.g.2.bc exists in the checked database.",
      "limit": "Linked-stage pointer syntax is not post-check syntax. Text counts are structural observations, not numerical reachability, alias proofs, or RTL equivalence."
