  "narrow_next_decision_advice": {
    "preferred_review_candidate": "If the main reviewer chooses a new source identity, isolate explicit aggregate initialization of the wrapper-local FullMemory: initialize all 26 existing pointer/capacity fields in declaration order to exactly their existing final values instead of invoking the default constructor then assigning five bindings. Keep Controller placement, helper bodies/calls, BEGIN/RUN branches, cleanup and task sequence unchanged. C++17 is already selected and FullMemory is an aggregate with only public fields/default member initializers. This is a proposal only; no source was edited or compiled.",
    "why_this_factor": "It directly targets the observed difference between constructor treatment in reflow-disaggr and late reflow-inliner without simultaneously changing protocol control flow or run_task wrappers. The prediction is about removing the constructor-call boundary in frontend/linked IR, not a claim that this will fix HLS.",
