    "secondary_candidate_only_separately": "Controller lifetime/control-flow placement may be tested later as a separate factor. BEGIN pending rejection must still perform no cleanup; parse-failure cleanup must retain current first-error/cleanup/report behavior; RUN and invalid-command paths must retain pending handling. Simply moving one declaration after parse is not valid because RUN does not parse again. Do not combine this with initialization and helper rewrites in one attempt.",
    "better_evidence_if_available_later": "A retained IR snapshot immediately before reflow-syncheck or after aggregate disaggregation, including member-pointer load/store operands and FullMemory address escapes, would distinguish true pointer alias obstruction from missed simplification. It is absent from the inspected Attention database. Capturing/replaying compiler passes would be a new tool action outside this review; successful I-L/I-V later IR cannot substitute for the failed check-stage snapshot.",
